ArrayProofs.bit_length_contract → <[T] as bit_field::BitArray<T>>::bit_length
  precondition: The translated BitField::BIT_LENGTH constant returns its declared width normally. Arbitrary element type, width and finite slice on x86_64; success and integer-overflow failure are both specified for the product.
  evidence: https://github.com/nyuichi/rust-crate-proofs/blob/acc19f974aef54ac200709255cbe40eb1de757e5/bit_field/0.10.3/aeneas/2026-11-05/proofs/ArrayProofs.lean#L1-L51
ArrayBitsProofs.get_bit_contract → <[T] as bit_field::BitArray<T>>::get_bit
  precondition: The BitField constant returns its declared width normally, and per-element get_bit/set_bit satisfy the explicit normal-return observation/update contracts at valid local indices. Arbitrary type, slice, index and set boolean; zero-width and out-of-bounds failures are also specified. This is a callback-conditional composition proof, not a body proof of arbitrary downstream implementations.
  evidence: https://github.com/nyuichi/rust-crate-proofs/blob/acc19f974aef54ac200709255cbe40eb1de757e5/bit_field/0.10.3/aeneas/2026-11-05/proofs/ArrayBitsProofs.lean#L1-L162
